\ls36\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Separate calibration data from evaluation data.\
\ls36\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Use walk-forward testing and prevent information leakage.\
\ls36\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Track predictions against realized costs and adverse movements.\
\ls36\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Test across route, asset, size, volatility, liquidity, and timing regimes.\
\ls36\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Publish model versions and change logs.\
\ls36\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Require review and approval before new parameters control live reserve trades.\
\pard\intbl\itap2\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Do not automatically reduce protection margins simply because a short period of execution outcomes appears favorable.\
\pard\intbl\itap2\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
