\fs48 \cf2 \cb1 Part K \'97 Final statement\
\pard\intbl\itap5\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 v5.0 is the correct architectural and process mandate. It is honest about status, rigorous about gates, and clear about what is and is not authorized.\
But v5.0 alone will produce a system with:\
\pard\intbl\itap5\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls75\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Reentrancy exposure (no guards specified).\
\ls75\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Silent precision issues in slippage (no unit clarity).\
\ls75\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
No path to recover stuck funds (no rescue path).\
\ls75\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Undefined behavior on multi-leg failure (no atomicity specification).\
\ls75\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
No escalation levels for oracle failure (no circuit breakers).\
\ls75\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
No formal invariants to detect corruption (no testable invariant set).\
\ls75\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
No deployment or upgrade discipline (no ordering, no upgradeability choice).\
\ls75\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
No mock infrastructure (tests cannot run).\
\pard\intbl\itap5\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 This extension closes those gaps. It does not add scope; it makes the existing scope implementable.\
The developer should implement v5.0 + this extension together. Neither is complete without the other. Neither authorizes production. Both are testnet-only until the gates close.\
\pard\intbl\itap5\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
