\fs44 \cf2 \cb1 Honest acknowledgment: what v5.0 + Extension 1 still do not cover\
\pard\intbl\itap2\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 v5.0 and Extension 1 focus on MARP execution protection \'97 the trades that rebalance the reserve. That focus is correct given where the P0 defects were found. But it means v5.0 + Extension 1 do not fully cover the rest of the Master Blueprint, and a developer handing off v5.0 + Extension 1 alone will produce a system that:\
\pard\intbl\itap2\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls76\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Cannot compute the Reserve Ratio from first principles (\'a7Part B).\
\ls76\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Has no Daily State Vector to feed the risk state machine (\'a7Part C).\
\ls76\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Has no Asset Admission Registry to govern which tokens the reserve can hold (\'a7Part D).\
\ls76\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Has no Geopolitical Eject mechanism for de-pegged assets (\'a7Part E).\
\ls76\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Has no Genesis Reserve, Cold Treasury, or replenishment procedure (\'a7Part F).\
\ls76\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Has no MEV protection for its own rebalances (\'a7Part G).\
\ls76\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Has no handling for paused, blacklisting, rebasing, or upgradeable tokens in its reserve (\'a7Part H).\
\pard\intbl\itap2\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 These are not optional. They are the operating system that the MARP execution engine sits inside. Without them, the corrected MARP trades assets that are governed by undefined rules, priced by undefined NAV, and reported in an undefined state vector.\
Extension 2 closes these gaps. It does not cover everything in the Master Blueprint \'97 some items are legitimately deferred to Gate 5 or Gate 7 \'97 but it covers what must exist for Gate 1 and Gate 2 to be meaningful.\
\pard\intbl\itap2\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 \
\pard\intbl\itap2\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs44 \cf2 \cb1 How to use this extension\
\pard\intbl\itap2\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 v5.0 = the MARP execution mandate.\uc0\u8232 Extension 1 = the contract-level safety and process extensions.\u8232 Extension 2 = the reserve, governance, oracle, MEV, and operational layer that the MARP engine depends on.\
The developer should read them in order. v5.0 defines what to trade. Extension 1 defines how to trade safely. Extension 2 defines what is being traded, what its value is, and what governs it.\
\pard\intbl\itap2\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
