\fs32 \cf2 Source: Master Blueprint \'a712.6 (previously under-specified)\uc0\u8232 Gap: v5.0 mentions "private-mempool or equivalent transaction-submission protections" but does not specify the mechanism, per-chain.\

\fs44 G.1 Why this matters\

\fs32 Every MARP rebalance is a public signal. Without MEV protection:\
\pard\intbl\itap4\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls95\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Front-running: An attacker sees the pending rebalance and trades ahead of it, moving the price.\
\ls95\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Sandwich attack: An attacker places a buy before and a sell after the rebalance, capturing the price impact.\
\ls95\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Back-running: An attacker extracts value from the post-trade state.\
\pard\intbl\itap4\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 The slippage guard (Extension 1 A.5) limits the loss per trade. But without MEV protection, the attacker simply extracts repeatedly until the slippage guard binds.\

