MARP cannot function without MASE. The direction-aware deviation (v5.0 Listing C-1) needs a target weight 
\f1\fs28 \cb5 targetW
\f0\fs32 \cb1 . That target comes from MASE. If MASE is not implemented, MARP has nothing to rebalance toward.\
Also important: v5.0 \'a73.5 defines 
\f1\fs28 \cb5 J(s)
\f0\fs32 \cb1  as the MARP trade-level economic objective. This is not the same as MASE's portfolio-level objective (Master Blueprint \'a77.4, the 8-term objective). Confusing them will produce a wrong implementation.\
