\fs32 \cf2 The gap: v5.0 and extensions treat MTQ as ERC-20 but do not specify:\
\pard\intbl\itap2\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls142\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Does MTQ use ERC-20 Permits (EIP-2612)?\
\ls142\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Does MTQ implement ERC-20 Votes / Snapshots (for governance)?\
\ls142\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Does MTQ have transfer restrictions?\
\ls142\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Does MTQ have a supply cap? If so, who can change it?\
\ls142\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Is MTQ upgradeable? (Extension 1 E.3 addresses this generally, but not for the token specifically.)\
\pard\intbl\itap2\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 These are not just nice-to-haves:\
\pard\intbl\itap2\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls143\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Permits affect gas costs and UX. Without them, every mint/redeem requires a separate approve transaction.\
\ls143\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Snapshots affect whether on-chain governance can measure voting power at historical blocks.\
\ls143\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Transfer restrictions affect whether the token is freely transferable or subject to whitelisting / KYC.\
\ls143\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Supply cap affects the monetary invariants and the "1 MTQ represents one basket unit" promise.\
\pard\intbl\itap2\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Recommended baseline (to be approved by Committee):\
\pard\intbl\itap2\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls144\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
MTQ is ERC-20 with ERC-20 Permits (EIP-2612) for UX.\
\ls144\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
MTQ is ERC-20 Votes / Snapshots for governance.\
\ls144\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
No transfer restrictions on public transfer (subject to legal review).\
\ls144\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Supply cap: no fixed cap initially; supply controlled by mint/burn at reference price. Cap policy is OD-29.\
\ls144\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Upgradeable: no (per Extension 1 E.3 Option A recommendation for the token itself).\
\pard\intbl\itap2\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Required: OD-37 \'97 Confirm MTQ token standard (Permits, Snapshots, transfer restrictions, supply cap, upgradeability) before any production authorization.\
Owner: Committee + Legal. Blocks: Gate 5.\
